# CRM (Vite SPA) — environment
#
# Copy to .env for local overrides, or .env.production for a production build.
# BOTH ARE OPTIONAL: every value below has a default that is already correct for
# the standard deployment, which is why scripts/deploy.sh does not require them.

# Origin the CRM API is reached at. LEAVE BLANK in production.
#
# Blank means the client issues relative requests — /crm/api/... and a Socket.IO
# handshake on the current origin — which is exactly right on
# https://cocomadigital.com, where Apache serves the SPA at /crm and proxies
# /crm/api and /crm/socket.io to the Express app on :5000. Same origin also
# means no CORS preflight on any API call, and no third-party-cookie questions.
#
# Set it ONLY if the SPA and the API are served from different origins, e.g. a
# staging SPA pointed at production data:
#   VITE_CRM_API_URL=https://cocomadigital.com
#
# Note the API paths in src/ already carry the /crm/api prefix, so this is an
# ORIGIN, not a base path — no trailing slash, no path segment.
VITE_CRM_API_URL=
